{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T082714Z_dev-05_staged_22f0", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "The paper does not give a detection significance for the GCE, either in σ or as a test statistic. It says the fitted GCE flux stays nonzero in all 80 diffuse-emission models, but adds that \"this observation alone does not establish its statistical significance.\" It also says the Δ(−2lnL) differences between diffuse models cannot be read as squared Gaussian significances, because the models are not nested. The only fit statistics it reports are χ² values for the dark-matter spectral fits, for example 22.82 for 12 degrees of freedom for τ⁺τ⁻. These measure how well each channel fits the GCE spectrum. They are not a detection significance for the excess. I did not read every section (for example the dSph sections 4 and 7), so a significance stated there is possible but unlikely.", "found": false, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "6.1"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "8"}]}, "turns": 10, "seconds": 20.388, "tool_calls": 11, "tool_result_chars": 61546, "input_tokens": 22, "output_tokens": 1450, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 21737, "cache_read_input_tokens": 150616, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:27:35+00:00"}
